# Generated from the OSRS Wiki page "Transcript:Sea Slug" by tools/quests/transcript_to_dialogue.py
0	section	Starting off
1	line	Player	Hello there.
1	line	Caroline	Is there any chance you could help me?
1	line	Player	What's wrong?
1	line	Caroline	It's my husband, he works on a fishing platform. Once a month he takes our son, Kennith, out with him.
1	line	Caroline	They usually write to me regularly, but I've heard nothing all week. It's very strange.
1	line	Player	Maybe the post was lost!
1	line	Caroline	Maybe, but no-one's heard from the other fishermen on the platform. Their families are becoming quite concerned.
1	line	Caroline	Is there any chance you could visit the platform and find out what's going on?
1	cond	If the player's Firemaking level is less than 30:
2	box	Before starting this quest, be aware that one or more of your skill levels are lower than what is required to fully complete it.
2	action	continues
1	cond	If the player's Firemaking level is 30 or above:
2	select	Start the Sea Slug quest?
2	option	Yes.
3	line	Player	I suppose so, how do I get there?
3	line	Caroline	That's very good of you {player}. My friend Holgart will take you there.
3	line	Player	Ok, I'll go and see if they're ok.
3	line	Caroline	I'll reward you for your time. It'll give me peace of mind to know Kennith and my husband, Kent, are safe.
3	action	end
2	option	No.
3	line	Player	I'm sorry, I'm too busy.
3	line	Caroline	That's a shame.
3	line	Player	Bye.
3	line	Caroline	Bye.
3	action	end
0	section	Talking to Caroline again
1	line	Player	Hello Caroline.
1	line	Caroline	Brave {player}, have you any news about my son and his father?
1	line	Player	I'm working on it now Caroline.
1	line	Caroline	Please bring them back safe and sound.
1	line	Player	I'll do my best.
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to Holgart
1	line	Player	Hello.
1	line	Holgart	Hello m'hearty.
1	line	Player	I would like a ride on your boat to the fishing platform.
1	line	Holgart	I'm afraid it isn't sea worthy, it's full of holes. To fill the holes I'll need some swamp paste.
1	line	Player	Swamp paste?
1	line	Holgart	Yes, swamp tar mixed with flour and heated over a fire.
1	cond	If the player already has one swamp paste in their inventory:
2	line	Holgart	In fact, unless me nose be mistaken, you've got some in yer pack.
2	line	Player	Oh yes, I forgot about that stuff. Can you use it?
2	line	Holgart	Aye, that be perfect.
2	line	Holgart	Right me hearty. Let's get this boat fixed.
2	line	Holgart	Huzzah! We've fixed the leaky old tub.
2	action	end
1	cond	If the player does not have swamp tar:
2	line	Player	Where can I find swamp tar?
2	line	Holgart	Unfortunately the only supply of swamp tar is in the swamps below Lumbridge. It's too far for an old man like me to travel.
2	line	Holgart	If you make me some swamp paste I'll give you a ride in my boat.
2	line	Player	I'll see what I can do.
2	action	end
0	section	Talking to Holgart again
1	line	Player	Hello Holgart.
1	line	Holgart	Hello m'hearty. Did you manage to make some swamp paste?
1	cond	If the player does not have swamp tar:
2	line	Player	I'm afraid not.
2	line	Holgart	It's simply swamp tar mixed with flour heated over a fire. Unfortunately the only supply of swamp tar is in the swamps below Lumbridge.
2	line	Holgart	I can't fix my row boat without it.
2	line	Player	Ok, I'll try to find some.
2	action	end
1	cond	If the player has swamp tar:
2	line	Player	Yes, I have some here.
2	line	Holgart	Right me hearty. Let's get this boat fixed.
2	line	Holgart	Huzzah! We've fixed the leaky old tub.
2	action	end
0	section	Talking to Holgart after fixing the boat
1	line	Player	Hello Holgart.
1	line	Holgart	Hello again land lover. There's some strange goings on, on that platform, I tell you.
1	select	Select an option
1	option	Will you take me there?
2	line	Player	Will you take me there?
2	line	Holgart	Of course m'hearty. If that's what you want.
2	box	You arrive at the fishing platform.
