0	section	Talking to Bailey
1	line	Player	Hello there.
1	line	Bailey	What? Who are you? Come inside quickly!
1	line	Bailey	What are you doing here?
1	line	Player	I'm trying to find out what happened to a boy named Kennith.
1	line	Bailey	Oh you mean Kent's son. He's around somewhere, probably hiding if he knows what's good for him.
1	line	Player	Hiding from what? What's got you so frightened?
1	line	Bailey	Haven't you seen all those things out there?
1	line	Player	The sea slugs?
1	line	Bailey	It all began about a week ago. We pulled up a haul of deep sea flatfish. Mixed in with them we found those slug things, but thought nothing of it.
1	line	Bailey	Not long after that my friends began to change, now they spend all day pulling in hauls of fish, only to throw back the fish and keep those nasty sea slugs.
1	line	Bailey	What am I supposed to do with those? I haven't figured out how to kill one yet, if I put them near the stove they squirm and jump away.
1	line	Player	I doubt they would taste too good.
1	line	Bailey	This is no time for humour.
1	line	Player	I'm sorry, I didn't mean to upset you.
1	line	Bailey	That's okay. I just can't shake the feeling that this is the start of something... Terrible.
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to Kennith
1	line	Player	Are you okay young one?
1	line	Kennith	No, I want my daddy!
1	line	Player	Where is your father?
1	line	Kennith	He went to get help days ago.
1	line	Kennith	The nasty fishermen tried to throw me and daddy into the sea. So he told me to hide here.
1	line	Player	That's good advice, you stay here and I'll go try and find your father.
1	action	end
0	section	Subsequent dialogue with Kennith
1	line	Player	Are you okay?
1	line	Kennith	I want to see daddy!
1	line	Player	I'm working on it.
1	action	end
1	cond	If the player kicks the loose panel near Kennith:
2	action	end
0	section	Talking to Holgart after talking to Kennith
1	line	Player	Holgart, something strange is going on here.
1	line	Holgart	You're telling me, none of the sailors seem to remember who I am.
1	line	Player	Apparently Kennith's father left for help a couple of days ago.
1	line	Holgart	That's a worry, no-one's heard from him on shore. Come on, we'd better go look for him.
1	box	You arrive on a small island.
1	action	end
0	section	At the shipwreck island
0	section	Talking to Holgart
1	line	Player	Where are we?
1	line	Holgart	Someway off mainland still. You'd better see if me old matey's okay.
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to Kent
1	line	Kent	Oh thank Saradomin! I thought I'd be left out here forever.
1	line	Player	Your wife sent me out to find you and your boy. Kennith's fine by the way, he's on the platform.
1	line	Kent	I knew the row boat wasn't sea worthy. I couldn't risk bringing him along but you must get him off that platform.
1	line	Player	What's going on here?
1	line	Kent	Five days ago we pulled in a huge catch. As well as fish we caught small slug like creatures, hundreds of them.
1	line	Kent	That's when the fishermen began to act strange.
1	line	Kent	It was the sea slugs, they attach themselves to your body and somehow take over the mind of the carrier.
1	line	Kent	I told Kennith to hide until I returned but I was washed up here.
1	line	Kent	Please go back and get my boy, you can send help for me later.
1	action	Kent notices a sea slug in your torso.
1	line	Kent	{player} wait!
1	line	Kent	A few more minutes and that thing would have full control of your body.
1	line	Player	Yuck! Thanks Kent.
1	action	end
0	section	Subsequent dialogue with Kent
1	line	Player	Hello.
1	line	Kent	Oh my, I must get back to shore.
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to Holgart again before returning to the fishing platform
1	line	Player	We'd better get back to the platform so we can see what's going on.
1	line	Holgart	You're right. It all sounds pretty creepy.
1	box	You arrive at the fishing platform.
1	action	end
